meta {
  name: ReserveringBevestigDoubleCallOvercounts
  type: http
  seq: 73
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/bon/{{bevestigBonnr}}/lijn/{{bevestigLijnnr}}/reservering/bevestig
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.gereserv: eq 1
}

docs {
  bon-auto-reservering design doc section 2.1 - documents the ACCEPTED trade-off
  of the all-or-nothing/non-idempotent confirm design, it is NOT a
  pass/fail regression gate for "correct" behaviour. Calls
  .../reservering/bevestig a SECOND time on the same
  {{bevestigBonnr}}/{{bevestigLijnnr}} line (already confirmed by
  ReserveringBevestigHappyPath) and still gets a plain 200 - there is no
  stored field to detect "already confirmed" (Marc rejected the
  bonlijn.gereserv-bevestigd field), so artikel.gereserveerd silently
  over-counts by the full bonlijn.gereserv amount a second time. That
  over-count is not independently observable through the documented HTTP
  contract - confirmed via direct ABL/DB query during backend-coder
  implementation (artikel.gereserveerd incremented by 1 twice, i.e. by 2
  total, for a line whose true entitlement is 1). See design doc section 2.1 for
  why this is a known, accepted limitation, not a bug to fix here.
}
